.TH ESHEEP 1 "August 2026" "linux-esheep 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
esheep \- a small animated desktop sheep
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esheep
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
eSheep walks across the monitor workarea and, on X11, can land on visible
application windows and panels. Left-click and drag moves the sheep. A
double-click makes it jump. Right-click opens the pet menu. When a legacy
status area is available, the single linux-esheep tray icon provides
group-wide show/hide, pause/resume, bring-to-front, About, and Quit actions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B --version
Show the program version.
.TP
.BI --sprite\  PATH
Use the specified spritesheet.
.TP
.BI --character\  NAME
Select the bundled sheep or ice-blue penguin character.
.TP
.BI --config\  PATH
Load settings from an INI config file.
.TP
.BI --spawn\  MODE
Use \fBbottom\fR (default), \fBwindow\fR, or \fBrandom\fR startup placement.
.TP
.BI --count\  N
Spawn 1 to 32 independent sheep.
.TP
.B --no-window-landing
Disable X11 window and panel detection.
.TP
.B --allow-conky
Allow Conky windows as landing surfaces.
.TP
.B --x11-fallback
Use the XWayland-backed GTK X11 backend when running under Wayland.
.TP
.BI --tick-ms\  N
Set the update interval from 10 to 1000 milliseconds.
.TP
.BI --walk-keep\  N
Set the floor walk keep-walking probability from 0 to 100. The original value
is 90.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ESHEEP_SPRITESHEET
Default spritesheet path.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_CHARACTER
Select \fBsheep\fR or \fBpenguin\fR when no explicit spritesheet is supplied.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_TICK_MS
Default update interval.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_WINDOW_LANDING
Set to 0 to disable X11 landing.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_EXCLUDE_CONKY
Set to 0 to allow Conky landing.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_X11_FALLBACK
Set to 1 to select the X11 backend through XWayland when available.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_SPAWN
Set to \fBwindow\fR to start on an application window.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_COUNT
Set the number of sheep, from 1 to 32.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_WALK_KEEP_PROBABILITY
Set the floor walk keep-walking probability from 0 to 100.
.SH NOTES
Window discovery and arbitrary popup positioning are available through the X11
backend. Native Wayland sessions require compositor-specific protocols; when
XWayland is available, use \fB--x11-fallback\fR.
The optional default config file is \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/esheep/config\fR and
uses an \fB[esheep]\fR INI section. Configuration is overridden by environment
variables and then command-line options.
.PP
Autostart is opt-in. Use the packaged XDG autostart entry through
Bmake install-autostartR; a normal installation does not enable it.
